<title>NORWAY: FORECAST - DnB Q1 profits seen down.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - DnB Q1 profits seen down.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske Bank, Norway's biggest bank, is expected to book pre-tax operating profits of 698 million crowns in the first quarter, down from 783 million in the same period last year, according to a consensus forecast by seven analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>Five analysts recommended to buy the share, while two said hold.</p>
<p>Estimates on Earnings Per Share varied because analysts had different assumptions on whether DnB will win a dispute with the authorities on tax losses carried forward from its crisis years around 1990.</p>
<p>DnB will present the first-quarter result at 0700 GMT on Tuesday.</p>
<p>					    Three months to March 31</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>				     average   high    low	Q1 96</p>
<p> Net interest income	  1,087     1,150  1,030    1,069</p>
